Review the [template guide](https://t-squared.seedcase-project.org/docs/guide/next-steps)
for more information on how to use the template and the next steps after copying
the project.

Next, run these commands in the terminal while inside of the project's
directory. Either use your system's terminal or use the built-in terminal in VS
Code, Positron, or RStudio:

- `git init -b main` to create the project as a Git repository.
- (If you installed just) `just list-todos` and complete all the TODO items.
- (If you installed just) `just build-readme` to build the Markdown version of the README from the Quarto version.

After going through all the TODO items and doing these tasks, add and commit the
files into the Git history.

{% if for_seedcase -%}

For Seedcase specific stuff (including with the
[spaid](https://github.com/seedcase-project/spaid) helper tool):

- `just update-quarto-theme` to update the rostools Quarto extension.
- `spaid_gh_create_repo_from_local {{ github_user }} {{ github_repo }} "DESCRIPTION"`
  to create a GitHub repository from the local repository (replace `DESCRIPTION`
  with a description of the workshop).
- `spaid_gh_set_repo_settings {{ github_repo_spec }}` to set the repository
  settings.
- `spaid_gh_ruleset_basic_protect_main {{ github_repo_spec }}` to protect the
  main branch.
- `spaid_gh_ruleset_require_pr {{ github_repo_spec }}` to require pull requests
  for changes to the main branch.
- Install or add the
  [auto-release-token](https://github.com/apps/auto-release-token) and
  [add-to-board-token](https://github.com/apps/add-to-board-token) GitHub Apps
  - Create an `UPDATE_VERSION_TOKEN` and `ADD_TO_BOARD_TOKEN` secret for the
    GitHub Apps if you haven't already and connect them to the repository.
  - Create an `UPDATE_VERSION_APP_ID` and `ADD_TO_BOARD_APP_ID` variable of the
    GitHub Apps' IDs if you haven't already and connect them to the repository.

{%- else -%}

To get the repository up on GitHub use the [gh CLI](https://cli.github.com/) to
create the GitHub repository from the terminal with:

```text
gh repo create {{ github_repo_spec }} --source=. --public --push
```

{%- endif %}

{% if hosting_provider == "netlify" -%}

If you use [Netlify](https://netlify.com), connect the repository to Netlify and
turn off the builds on Netlify, since you will be using GitHub Actions to build
and deploy the website. The [guide](https://t-squared.seedcase-project.org/docs/guide/next-steps)
describes this in more detail.

{%- elif hosting_provider == "gh-pages" %}

If you will be using GitHub pages, run `quarto publish gh-pages` to setup and
start publishing the website to GitHub Pages.

{%- endif %}

Finally, some optional tasks:

- `just install-precommit` to install the pre-commit hooks.
- If relevant, connect [GoatCounter](https://www.goatcounter.com/).
- If relevant, connect [pre-commit.ci](https://pre-commit.ci/) to the repository
  and enable the pre-commit hooks.
